{"qid":"Q1045","names":["Federal Republic of Somalia","People's Democratic Republic of Yemen"],"title":"Federal Republic of Somalia","endonym":{"native":"جمهورية الصومال الفدرالية","lang":"ar"},"capsule":"Somalia gained independence on 1 July 1960 when the Trust Territory of Somalia (formerly Italian Somalia) united with the British Somaliland Protectorate to form the Somali Republic; the dataset's from-year of 1960 reflects this foundation, while the nominal to-year of 2025 spans the Federal Government of Somalia formally constituted in 2012. The civilian parliamentary republic collapsed when General Mohamed Siad Barre staged a coup in 1969, proclaiming scientific socialism; his regime fell in January 1991, triggering state collapse, clan warfare, and a humanitarian catastrophe that prompted the UN Operation in Somalia (UNOSOM) intervention in 1992–1995. A Federal Government was re-established in Mogadishu in 2012, but the Al-Shabaab insurgency retains control over large rural areas as of the mid-2020s.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Nominal borders are established by UN recognition, but effective governmental control has been highly fragmentary since 1991; territorial extent of the federal government versus clan-controlled and Al-Shabaab zones is fluid.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Somalia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Somalia"},{"label":"Britannica: Somalia","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Somalia"}],"britannica":"place/Somalia","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Somalia","rulers":[{"qid":"Q317806","name":"Abdullahi Issa","start":1956,"end":1960,"image":"Abdullahi Issa Mo